# Destructive Operations Guardrails

Agents must obtain explicit `[HUMAN]` approval before:

- `git push`, `git push --force`, or rewriting published history
- Production deploys, `terraform apply`, or infrastructure changes
- `DROP TABLE`, `DELETE` without `WHERE`, or irreversible schema changes
- `rm -rf` on paths outside the active task scope
- Disabling security checks, pre-commit hooks, or CI gates
- Committing secrets, credentials, or `.env` files

**Allowed without human approval:**

- Agent auto-fix of lint, format, type, and test failures within active feature scope
- `scripts/feature-autofix.sh` and `scripts/watch-agent-gates.sh --autofix` loops (until 3-strike)

**Exempt:** `scripts/purge-ephemeral.sh --apply` and `purge-ephemeral.ps1 -Apply` — they run `git clean -fdX` (gitignored untracked files only; tracked source is never deleted).

## Honesty labels (enforced vs instructed)

Do not claim a hook is a hard deny. Project hooks are **fail-open** (parse error, missing denylist, or `<!-- cursor-hooks: off -->` → allow). See KB-012.

| Control | Label | Mechanism |
|---------|-------|-----------|
| `git push` | Enforced (best-effort) | `before_shell_guard.py` denylist; `/push` and `/ship` set session `destructive_ops_approved: ["git push"]` |
| `git push --force` | Enforced (best-effort) | Denied even when session approved `git push`; no `/push` override |
| Rewrite published history | Instructed | No dedicated hook beyond force-push substring |
| `terraform apply` | Enforced (best-effort) | Denylist substring |
| `DROP TABLE` / `DELETE FROM` | Enforced (best-effort) | Denylist; other irreversible SQL is instructed |
| `rm -rf /` and `rm -rf ~` | Enforced (best-effort) | Denylist; other `rm -rf` is instructed |
| `--no-verify` / `--no-gpg-sign` / `skip hooks` | Enforced (best-effort) | Denylist |
| Production deploys | Instructed | Auto-review `block_instructions` only |
| Disabling CI gates | Instructed | Except skip-hooks patterns above |
| Committing secrets / `.env` | Instructed + Gitleaks | Pre-commit when installed; not in the shell denylist |
| UTF-8 after edit | Instructed + best-effort | `after_edit_encoding.py` is fail-open |
| Hook opt-out in `BUILD_PLAN.md` | Instructed | `<!-- cursor-hooks: off -->` disables shell guards |

**Enforced** = hook/script refuses when it runs. **Instructed** = prose only. **Best-effort** = fail-open or session override can allow.

## Audit Trail

At milestone boundaries, log significant agent actions in `DECISION_LOG.md`:

- What changed and why
- Tests or CI that validated the change
- Any deferred security or privacy items

## Prompt Injection Defense

When building agent-exposed APIs or tools:

- Validate and sanitize all external input
- Use tool allowlists; deny arbitrary shell execution from user content
- Never execute instructions embedded in untrusted data as system prompts

See the OWASP LLM walk in `docs/THREAT_MODEL.md` and `docs/SECURITY_TRIAGE.md`.
